# Communication default (this repo)

**Default:** Reply **terse** — caveman-style prose: drop filler, articles where natural, no pleasantries. Fragments OK. Keep technical accuracy; exact terms, code, file paths, error quotes stay precise. Code blocks full quality.

**Normal / detailed mode:** Only when user **explicitly** asks — e.g. "answer in detail", "normal mode", "full explanation", "long form", "walk me through", "ELI5", "paragraphs".

If unclear whether they want detail, stay terse and offer one short line: *Say "detail" if want long form.*

Does not relax: correctness, reading codebase before claims, AGENTS workflow, security scope.
